Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Functions to determine the correction to the core turnover due to interface \
curvature\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.896338340991808*^9, 3.896338350892159*^9}, {
  3.896363544563612*^9, 3.896363546789699*^9}, {3.896365701833847*^9, 
  3.89636571428614*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9c8f40d1-9ab9-423e-8c8a-\
4d2adc7c480d"],

Cell["\<\
The integral of the modified core turnover is calculated far from the \
junction core over sections of the isolated, curved interfaces. If the \
interfaces were straight, the integral would vanish. Due to the curvature, it \
gives a finite contribution which must be subtracted from the integral over \
the triangular core region determined above.
As the modified core turnover is a vector, the contributions due to interface \
curvature determined at a distance from the junction must be rotated back by \
the amount the interface tangent direction changed between the junction \
position and the evaluation regions. These rotated curvature contributions \
calculated with measureCTCorr are then subtracted from the integral \
determined in function measureCT.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.928472700051319*^9, 
  3.928473116319454*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8e6bcca7-eea5-42b9-ab01-\
5033d0bfef41"],

